From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: Allow cross-thread cancellation of windowless timers.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Windows 10 x64 assigns distinct IDs to live windowless timers on different
threads of a process. KillTimer(NULL, id) cancels the requested timer even
from another thread, without cancelling the caller's timer.

Wine only searched the calling queue, which could either reject a valid
ID or cancel the wrong timer when two queues assigned the same ID.

Make windowless ID allocation and cancellation process-wide. Leave
delivery on the owner queue, leave replacement on the creating queue,
and keep the existing behavior for windowed timers.

v1 2026-11-22: Matches the measured same-process Win32 cases.

v2 (2026-11-23): No code change. Its user32 test passed on Windows 10
(L1); promoted to the normal series after cross review and the AutoCAD
and Inventor smoke tests.

